<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:28Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Zelensky turns to Europe for backing as ties with Trump deteriorate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8a053260404649359999b533d34d365056e565326cfbba84078ba191634f388b</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T20:25:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-zelensky-turns-to-europe-for-backing-as-ties-with-trump-deteriorate" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky turned to his European allies on Friday, asking Brussels for an additional €70 billion to fund the war against Russia next year. Zelensky's relationship with US President Donald Trump deteriorated after the US eased sanctions on Moscow as part of a diesel-supply deal.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>KENYA CONFIRMS THIRD EBOLA CASE</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0a63fb14c79248864aa0718b62ff5c24c6f87b14949162c4d32465d5b92120cc</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T20:25:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/kenya-confirms-third-ebola-case" /><summary type="html">In tonight's programme, Kenya confirms a third case of Ebola, a relative of a man who died earlier this month after travelling from DR Congo. Also,Cameroonian journalist Ambe Macmillan is recovering in hospital after being shot in the legs by gunmen in Bamenda. And we meet Ghanaian artist Ibrahim Mahama... And finally, we meet Ghanaian artist Ibrahim Mahama, who digs deep into his country's colonial and industrial past to lay new creative foundations for generations to come.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>'Finish what we started': After student protests, France braces for return of the Yellow Vests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3a542baf41c4263a1ea0f280b65c08e26429ca71dcb8f38066378908dce59982</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T20:10:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-finish-what-we-started-after-student-protests-france-braces-return-yellow-vests" /><summary type="html">An online movement against rising fuel prices has gained momentum ahead of planned nationwide demonstrations on October 17 with former Yellow Vest figures set to join the protests in support of high-school students. Some are drawing parallels between the latest action and the 2018 cost-of-living protests that rattled President Emmanuel Macron's first term in office.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Clashes grip Tirana as Albanian PM blames 'foreign hands' for mounting unrest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8783941eb80f482a098b2379ccb4890d16aee99fa60789da1d8fd50a6e5e8edb</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T19:59:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-clashes-grip-tirana-as-albanian-pm-blames-foreign-hands" /><summary type="html">Albanian Prime Minister Edi Rama on Friday blamed the involvement of “foreign hands” for escalating protests, which he said are aimed at hindering Albania's bid to join the European Union. Thousands of demonstrators have taken to the streets of Albania's capital since Tuesday, demanding Rama’s resignation and denouncing university conditions and high tuition fees.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Trump Vs Zelensky, From the Screen to the Streets, Gen Z protests from Paris to Dehli</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:400a598a544049be7e3574e69620abcfdd29d3f2558377b4471ea4990e8e4809</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T19:21:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20261016-trump-vs-zelensky-from-the-screen-to-the-streets-gen-z-protests-from-paris-to-dehli" /><summary type="html">In India, the Cockroach movement felt the crushing boot of the state this week. Thousands of Gen Z protesters were rounded up and detained in sports stadiums and community halls turned into makeshift detention centres, while the movement’s founder, Abhijeet Dipke, was arrested on arrival. A mass demonstration over alleged voter fraud was effectively crushed before it could begin.And Abdijeet has been detained again todayNarendra Modi’s government says the measures were necessary to protect civilians in the capital. But he now faces accusations of choosing repression over democracy, with the UN Human Rights Office urging authorities to respect the right to peaceful assembly. 
 
 
 
It’s been a week of blame games and accusations of betrayal in Ukraine with President Zelensky speaking of his personal hurt at President Trump’s decision to make a diesel deal with the Kremlin ahead of the US Mid term elections calling it “weak”, suggesting Trump had chosen, “the other side”. Trump meanwhile made clear he wants Zelensky replaced, and warned him against striking Russian refineries AND announced an energy ceasefire, declaring it to have been agreed by both sides but which went nowhere. President Zelensky continued to search for solidarity and a solution in Europe.
 
 
 
It’s been a week of blame games and accusations of betrayal in Ukraine with President Zelensky speaking of his personal hurt at President Trump’s decision to make a diesel deal with the Kremlin ahead of the US Mid term elections calling it “weak”, suggesting Trump had chosen, “the other side”. Trump meanwhile made clear he wants Zelensky replaced, and warned him against striking Russian refineries AND announced an energy ceasefire, declaring it to have been agreed by both sides but which went nowhere. President Zelensky continued to search for solidarity and a solution in Europe. 
 
 
 
Gavin Lee is joined this week by Anne-Elisabeth Moutet, John Sweeney, Victor Mallet and Suhasini Raj.</summary><category term="The World This Week" /></entry><entry><title>'US tilting toward Russia: Europeans are standing more and more solidly with Zelensky'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ac28eba5dc33e48ffa44c5cc22645f603fea3ec697515946b79d8627f5dfe977</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T18:33:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261016-us-tilting-toward-russia-europeans-are-standing-more-and-more-solidly-with-zelensky" /><summary type="html">As transatlantic relations confront renewed geopolitical uncertainty, former Estonian President Toomas Hendrik Ilves delivers a pointed assessment of Washington's shifting approach to Russia's war on Ukraine and the profound implications for European security. At the heart of his analysis lies a fundamental question: can Europe develop the political unity, strategic independence and military capabilities necessary to defend its interests in an increasingly unpredictable international order?  Ilves response: "If there's any time for Europe to begin to act as Europe and not as being strictly self-interested, then this is the time for it."</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Sally Rooney's books no longer sold in UK over support for banned pro-Palestinian group</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:478eb5e60fd9629a595fc9265fa9b0dd3fcfbe5991ffbb2ca059afbea5cc88cd</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T16:26:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261016-sally-rooney-s-books-no-longer-sold-in-uk-over-support-for-banned-pro-palestinian-group" /><summary type="html">Irish novelist Sally ⁠Rooney's books will ​no longer be sold in Britain over her plans to use her royalties ​to support Palestine Action, a pro-Palestinian group banned as a terrorist organisation, Rooney and her publisher said on Wednesday. The bestselling author, known for novels including "Normal People" and "Conversations with ​Friends", has ‌been a vocal supporter of Palestine Action, including after ⁠it was proscribed by the British government under terrorism laws last year.</summary></entry><entry><title>Argentine demonstration over education cuts ends in clashes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fd7d6a9de20dd5414150ebfe5ea32d2f06aa2eb5238f66c40194729a0d0e3b87</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T16:25:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261016-argentine-demonstration-over-education-cuts-ends-in-clashes" /><summary type="html">Argentine demonstrators clashed with police on Thursday at a major protest in Buenos Aires over budget-slashing President Javier Milei's higher education spending. The main demonstration outside parliament by thousands of university students and staff, trade unionists and opposition activists remained peaceful. But dozens of mostly hooded demonstrators who broke away from the crowd lobbed stones and other projectiles at the police, who responded with tear gas and water cannons.</summary></entry><entry><title>Embattled new White House Press Secretary Zacharia 'let go' from her role</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a48ff069ff9ae4bf0c968876e95f45e66f65bca39d67caf027d1a94ce1fbb354</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T15:57:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261016-embattled-new-white-house-press-secretary-zacharia-let-go-from-her-role" /><summary type="html">A White House Press official said Friday that Secretary ​Katie Zacharia was "let go" from her role after US President Donald Trump signaled she was on her way out, a week after he picked her for the post. Zacharia's credentials as an attorney had come under scrutiny and she admitted to not having passed the bar in an interview with Fox News on Thursday.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>'Finish what we started': After student protests, France braces for return of the Yellow Vests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9e629a5bc5c1b2d2b1756b19c5f376091781662df880a74b1f18bbec1270147d</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T15:55:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261016-cost-of-living-demonstrations-to-grip-pre-election-france" /><summary type="html">An online movement against rising fuel prices has gained momentum ahead of planned nationwide demonstrations on October 17 with former Yellow Vest figures set to join the protests in support of high-school students. Some are drawing parallels between the latest action and the 2018 cost-of-living protests that rattled President Emmanuel Macron's first term in office.</summary></entry><entry><title>India detains top 'cockroach' leader as hundreds protest in capital</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b458eb84e8a3623287553b321a5c95157eda94701a09b3853e5a555e64728da2</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T15:53:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261016-india-detains-top-cockroach-leader-as-hundreds-protest-in-capital" /><summary type="html">Indian police detained Cockroach Janta Party (CJP) leader Abhijeet Dipke on Friday ahead of fresh protests demanding the removal of the country's election chief, the youth-led movement said in a social media post. Dipke, 31, was detained shortly before a rally called by the online movement in the heart of New Delhi where hundreds of protesters marched on Friday evening, despite heavy security measures. FRANCE 24's Navodita Kumari reports from New Delhi, India.</summary></entry><entry><title>Zelensky hails "real leaders" in Europe, blasts Trump's diesel deal with Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ece809aa3d40feab16211b8016fbdc8bc6a9709e767d2dc28ed241cfc1932c42</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T15:40:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261016-zelensky-hails-real-leaders-in-europe-blasts-trump-s-diesel-deal-with-russia" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian ​President Volodymyr Zelensky took aim on Friday at US President Donald Trump's diesel deal with Russia and welcomed the prospect of European allies stepping up their role in talks, calling Moscow's stance a "parody" of peace negotiations. At a European Union summit in Brussels, Zelenskiy said Russia did not want peace. He added that Ukraine was still experiencing disruptions to the SpaceX Starshield satellite system. FRANCE 24's Europe Editor Armen Georgian reports from Brussels.</summary></entry><entry><title>France braces for massive protests: Yellow Vests to join students on Saturday</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:661cb5b0d73a45714e1f120b8c67c5ead6fc07588df1ef77bf85b569e699f6e9</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T15:38:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261016-france-braces-for-massive-protests-yellow-vests-to-join-students-on-saturday" /><summary type="html">After weeks of student protests, France is set to be swept by broader, nationwide demonstrations on Saturday. The country's Yellow Vest movement – which eight years ago staged street protests against President Emmanuel Macron – has appealed to teachers, workers, pensioners and farmers, as well as students, in an online call spread through social media. The prospect of the two movements merging poses a big challenge to the government, as FRANCE 24’s Shirli Sitbon reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Italy prolongs Schengen suspension with Spain, talks loom</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:58849ef097eab87c5e0074898f8effc9bfd601ad09205ba1facaaa5c4c554117</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T15:37:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261016-italy-prolongs-schengen-suspension-with-spain-talks-loom" /><summary type="html">Italy has extended by another week ​its suspension of the European Union's border-free travel arrangements with Spain over a surge in migrant arrivals in Ceuta in late July, ​an ‌Italian government source said on Friday. A ⁠Spanish government spokesperson said the interior ministers of both countries would work over ‌the coming week on lifting the border controls.</summary></entry><entry><title>REPLAY: Ukraine's Zelensky holds presser in Brussels</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7b040a90c4cd4a0063ce627f768130bb78d167011c58bdb437937f405a8c01c2</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T15:36:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261016-replay-ukraine-s-zelensky-holds-presser-in-brussels" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky on Friday urged European leaders to maintain their support for Kyiv and warned against easing sanctions on Russia. Speaking to reporters at the European summit in Brussels, Zelensky said that ending the war remained Ukraine’s priority but accused Russian President Vladimir Putin of having no genuine interest in negotiations. He also criticised a US deal involving Russian diesel, arguing that easing restrictions could allow Moscow to reap financial benefits and pave the way for broader sanctions relief. Watch the replay.</summary></entry><entry><title>Indonesia's forest fires spark public health crisis across Southeast Asia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:74f27379b61b57a074eb0fc2df2daaee82994e66120d4b584d21e935c3a16d6a</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T15:26:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20261016-indonesia-s-forest-fires-spark-public-health-crisis-across-southeast-asia" /><summary type="html">Massive wildfires in Indonesia show no sign of letting up. The environmental disaster is turning into a pollution crisis across Southeast Asia, as toxic haze from the blazes spread to neighbouring countries.</summary><category term="Access Asia" /></entry><entry><title>The risks faced by women migrants in Europe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:77f951a0cf421b642e829e81d332fe86c4a95ba6d260a2a718527a8467a8901a</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T15:05:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261016-the-risks-faced-by-women-migrants-in-europe" /><summary type="html">This October marks 10 years since French police dismantled the notorious Calais "Jungle" camp. FRANCE 24's Claire Paccalin returns to the region to explore what has changed for migrants over the past decade. She joins Annette Young and Dr Marissa Quie of Cambridge University to discuss migration routes and their growing role in European political debate.</summary><category term="The 51%" /></entry><entry><title>US journalist injured during Israeli settler attack on West Bank olive harvest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be1b852b6f041fd1c4bfa4030d8beb5c614d3a858e9f887732d0f53db496f4fd</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T15:01:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261016-us-journalist-injured-during-israeli-settler-attack-on-west-bank-olive-harvest" /><summary type="html">About 80 Israeli settlers set fire to olive trees and threw stones at Palestinians in a West Bank village Friday, injuring at least two people, including a US photojournalist with The Washington Post. The coordinated attack came as violence by settlers is on the rise during the olive harvest in the occupied Palestinian territory.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Ibrahim Mahama's abundant artistic harvest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:588d1423195d0bed82ea96a5f1dfda463591de4ebcdad2cb92fd052525dc039f</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T14:55:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261016-ibrahim-mahama-s-abundant-artistic-harvest" /><summary type="html">His monumental installations excavate Ghana's past and build firm foundations for the country’s artistic future. Ibrahim Mahama has represented his country at the Venice Biennale and established three cultural hubs in northern Ghana, nurturing creative communities for generations to come.</summary><category term="arts24" /></entry><entry><title>South African rugby player Hyron ​Andrews dies in France ahead of Champions Cup debut</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7eb9ceac77fa3767a04b3b0692046f7acdceb760183277b94948db5dd91b24a6</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T13:40:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20261016-south-african-rugby-player-found-dead-in-french-hotel-ahead-of-champions-cup-debut" /><summary type="html">Hyron ​Andrews, a 31-year-old rugby player for the Lions team, was found dead at a hotel in France on Friday, the day before the South African club ​are due to play La Rochelle in the Champions Cup. The match will go ahead in his honour, his team said.</summary><category term="Sport" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia announces interim government in Tigray, aims for polls in six months</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1836ca529d647ae3cedc51fffba8776609edc77911e1b71f45580a9b7858bca4</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T13:05:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261016-ethiopia-announces-interim-government-tigray-calls-for-polls-six-months" /><summary type="html">Ethiopian Prime Minister Abiy Ahmed on Friday announced the appointment of an interim administration to prepare elections in the northern Tigray region previously controlled by the Tigray People's Liberation Front that has clashed with government forces since September. The recent conflict revived a war that killed hundreds of thousands between 2020 and 2022.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo XIV celebrates mass in hospital while recovering from lung cancer operation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5018e10fef7dbd725dc46dbd142ed4ddf5e2fa4007fc51f833ead9ddf2bde005</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T12:57:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-pope-leo-xiv-celebrates-mass-in-hospital-while-recovering-from-lung-cancer-operation" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo XIV celebrated a mass at Rome's Gemelli hospital Friday after undergoing surgery to remove a cancerous tumour from his right lung, photos released by the Vatican showed. Doctors said his recovery was progressing normally but that further tests would show whether the cancer had spread.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'America, with this president, is not our ally. Trump is a liar': French MEP Bernard Guetta</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:da2edcdf1b13d6da92aa312ac0d5910e7c9adb7f2434abe2fb013bc98f7e71df</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T12:55:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261016-america-with-this-president-is-not-our-ally-trump-is-a-liar-french-mep-bernard-guetta" /><summary type="html">Our guest is veteran French journalist and commentator Bernard Guetta, who is a Member of the European Parliament for the centrist Renew group. He tells the programme that Donald Trump is "a liar, because he tried to tell the American people that Zelensky and the Ukrainian resistance were responsible for the price of diesel. This is a pure lie. He (Trump) is responsible because he started the war with Iran." Guetta goes on to say that "without American intelligence sharing, Ukraine is weaker and weaker. That's terrible, to see the president of the United States giving a hand to Putin against Ukraine."</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Thanks a lot, Trump': Wyoming conservatives divided ahead of US midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b63a2f7cdbbc970d96dcee09f91f5cb6dc0e4b508759bcb4f8a9180f0df94f01</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T12:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20261016-thanks-a-lot-trump-wyoming-conservatives-divided-ahead-us-midterms" /><summary type="html">Famous for its cowboy culture, Wyoming is the least populated, the most rural and the most conservative of all the US states. With two weeks to go until the midterm elections, our reporters James André and Sylvain Rousseau travelled across this Republican stronghold and found that the party of US President Donald Trump is deeply divided in the Cowboy State.</summary><category term="Reporters" /></entry></feed>
